+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Product reviews currently expose private customer data, accept invalid ratings, allow duplicate or impersonated submissions, and can leave product aggregates stale after merchant changes. This change makes review behavior safe, consistent, and correct across the public and authenticated APIs.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Restrict public review responses to review id, rating, description, date, and reviewer first name only.
+- Enforce authenticated review ownership, one review per customer/product, and whole-number ratings from 1 through 5 with the specified HTTP errors.
+- Support merchant review updates and deletion with product-scoped not-found behavior.
+- Recalculate product rating and ratingCount after every review create, update, or delete, using one-decimal half-up rounding and zeroes when no reviews remain.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `product-reviews`: Privacy-safe product review reads, validated customer submissions, merchant lifecycle operations, and consistent product rating aggregates.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None.
+
+## Impact
+
+Affected Spring controllers and facades in `sm-shop`, review and product services in `sm-core`/`sm-core-modules`, API model/populator classes in `sm-shop-model` and `sm-shop`, and integration/unit tests covering the v1 review endpoints and v2 product representation. No external dependency is required.
